# HakiOS fragment: the Infinix Hot 20 (x6826b) -- what is true of this phone and of no other with an MT6768.
# Its touch screen (a TD4160 on SPI2, whose firmware mtkloader sends), and the arguments of the runs that work on it:
# the keypad and the big cores at speed, the Mali at 800 MHz (a higher clock raises VGPU and VSRAM_GPU further: not without
# the owner's yes), the panel's
# 720 x 1640 shown one pixel to a pixel at scale 2 (fbscale=2 fbfit=3) and flipped rather than copied over (fb_flip=1),
# surfaces as the Mali takes them, the accelerometer through the SCP. mtkloader adds the root (rd=md0 emmc_root=1).
CONFIG_DEVICE="x6826b"
CONFIG_HAKIOS_TCM=y
CONFIG_BUTTONS=2
CONFIG_MTK_CPUFREQ=3
CONFIG_MALI=y
CONFIG_MALI_MHZ=800
CONFIG_FBSCALE=2
CONFIG_FBFIT=3
CONFIG_FB_QUEUE=1
CONFIG_FB_FLIP=y
CONFIG_FB_INUSE=y
CONFIG_SURF_ALIGN=y
CONFIG_SURF_LOCKWAIT=y
CONFIG_SCP_STEP=7
CONFIG_BOOTARGS="touchscreen=2"
